WEBVTT

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:08.910
"Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger"

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.910
"Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger"
<i>Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger</i>!

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:17.950
♪ Their burning spirit roars!
Take off into outer space! ♪

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:24.040
♪ In travels, companionship;
in life, love & peace ♪

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.910
♪ Though we can warp past asteroids ♪

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:36.910
♪ it's another matter to cross outer space ♪

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:43.500
♪ Let's go! Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger! ♪

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.500
♪ Dan-Dan! Downing some dumplings ♪

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.500
♪ Jin-Jin! Paying visits to shrines ♪

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.450
♪ Gon-Gon! Rowing gondolas ♪

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:55.450
♪ Do! Do! Do-do-do! ♪

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.500
♪ Zun-Zun! Singing the Zundoko Bushi ♪

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.500
♪ Bun-Bun! Bunbuku Chagama ♪

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.370
--♪ Gen-Gen! A spirited "To the stars" ♪

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:04.450
--♪ Gen-Gen! A spirited "To the stars" ♪
--Hizakuriger!

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:10.950
--♪ Along a never-ending journey ♪
--Hizakuriger!

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.080
"We started making a long anime,"
"but the studio has yet to return our call"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.290
"It's almost as though they're
on a journey of adventure (sob)"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.410
"It's almost as though they're
on a journey of adventure (sob)"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.950
"Dream of the Moon, Dream of the Earth"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.660
A space fleet? But from where?

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.500
The moon. It's a lunar fleet.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.450
The moon? You mean Earth's moon?

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.160
They've come to get me.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.950
I'm... the prince of the moon, after all.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.200
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.250
Listen, I think we might have misheard you.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.290
Mm-hmm. Could you say
that again, just to be sure?

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:02.450
I said I'm the prince of the moon,
and that space fleet is here for me.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.540
Oh, yeah? Prince of the moon, huh?

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.750
Oho, they're here for the
prince of the moon, are they?

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.120
Huh?

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.450
Ah! Mr. Yang! Robby's ship is down there!

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.540
Put it on the main screen!

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.790
I've found you, Robby.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.370
So what'll it be, Robby?

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.910
Are you gonna stop by the priestess café
under these circumstances?

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.790
No way, I'm not about to let Yang catch me.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.450
So, what is the great prince
of the moon going to do?

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.500
Don't call me that.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.700
Okay, Hatchi, what do you want to do?

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.120
I'm asking you what you want.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:43.660
Well, I don't want that. I don't want
to go back until our journey is over.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:47.080
I want to see this journey through
to the end with you, Robby!

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.660
And you, too, of course, Ikku.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.080
Hatchi...

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.620
Hmm. Well, an excursion is still
an excursion until you get home.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.870
Let's go! We're sticking
together until the end!

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:00.870
Mm-hmm!

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.450
Yikes! Yang is heading this way!

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.040
Prince Hatchi located! He appears
to be boarding the red spaceship ahead.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.910
In the name of the Luna Guard,
we will bring Prince Hatchi back home.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.750
Ikku, emergency blastoff!

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:20.910
Roger!

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.120
Mr. Yang, Robby is getting away!

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.870
I can see that for myself!

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.750
--Mr. Yang!
--Now what?!

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.500
What's the story with that fleet?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.950
It's no use! They're overtaking!

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.200
The Luna Guard is exceptional, to be sure.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.080
Prepare to engage tractor beam!

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.160
Something is approaching
at high speed to port!

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.160
What?!

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.160
What the hell are you doing to my Robby?!

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.750
What the...?!

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.450
--Huh?!
--Exceptional, all right.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.200
Hurry and go after Robby!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.910
--Yes, Mr. Yang!
--Yes, Mr. Yang!

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.250
Ships 2 through 5 are out of commission!

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:11.700
Damn! We'll protect the prince,
even if we have to do it alone!

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.000
What are you waiting for?!
Hurry up and catch them!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.910
Hey, Ikku! You're just flying us
around Isekandar, aren't you?!

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.250
Get us out of here, already!

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.120
Where do you want us to run to?!

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.950
Back to Earth, obviously! This trip
isn't over until we get to Earth!

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.330
You make it sound so easy!

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.620
Do you realize how long it took
to get here from Earth?!

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.250
Huh? Is that...?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.200
--Huh?
--Robby's spaceship disappeared.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.330
Find it! It must still be in the area!

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.250
We managed to give them the slip.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.910
I'm parched.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.870
But we have to figure out
what we're going to do.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.660
It's only a matter of time before they find us.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.700
Nah, you're the real issue here, aren't you?

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:22.910
Hatchi,

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.950
things have been so hectic,
it almost slipped my mind,

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.200
but why is a prince on the run?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.500
Huh? Why, that's a great question.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.200
Actually, are you even
really prince of the moon?

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.040
You're sure you didn't commit
some crime and go on the lam?

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.500
No way!

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:42.040
I really am the prince of the moon! Look!

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:45.250
Let's see here, "Nationality: the moon;
Profession: prince."

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.540
Whoa! It says his profession is "prince"!

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.830
Heh, now that's rich.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:52.580
So, if you're a prince,
you must be loaded, right?

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:53.410
Huh?

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.870
Do you have any retainers?

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.120
How much is your allowance?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.790
Were you raised by a nanny or anything?

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.950
Your bank balance must be awesome, right?

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:01.200
What number in line to the throne are you?

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.950
Do you have a fiancée? Is she pretty?
Is she really pretty?!

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:07.000
If she has a pretty helper robot, introduce me.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.950
Screw you both!

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:11.330
Just because I'm a prince
doesn't mean anything!

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.620
Also, I don't have any more money
that I can freely withdraw.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.200
I used it up paying off your debt, Robby!

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.290
Huh? What did you just say?

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.290
Did you just say you paid off my debt?!

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:27.040
That explains it. So that's what happened.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.790
I've been wondering this whole time
how we passed that checkpoint

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:33.830
with Robby's name still on the blacklist.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:38.790
Turns out it's all because Hatchi
paid off Robby's debt for him.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.660
And since Robby used his Smartbracelet
to do a credit payment,

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.870
the moon folks found out where he was.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.540
Is that true?

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.080
Why'd you do it?

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.700
Well, because I wanted...

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:53.540
Hmm?

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.910
I said, you know, because I wanted...

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.040
Huh?

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.700
Because I wanted to go to Isekandar with you!

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:04.080
Hatchi, are you...?

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.080
I'm the prince of the moon,
so ever since I was little,

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.750
I've received a strict upbringing
to prepare me to be the king.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:16.450
Lessons in kingcraft and all other
subjects, plus self-defense training.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:20.250
Ah! That's why, back there...

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:25.120
Yeah. I had to acquire all that
knowledge in order to be the king.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.870
But then, why would the prince
of the moon go work for Yang?

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.910
Because I ran away from
the Luna Land embassy.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.160
"Reiwa"

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.370
"Reiwa"
I'd come to Earth for some kind of ceremony.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.250
I'd come to Earth for some kind of ceremony.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:49.450
So, I ended up taking a job at Yang's
Finance, and that was my first day.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:53.620
Oh, yeah? So the moon kingdom
has an embassy in Neo Tokyo?

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.450
Of course. The people of Luna Land
originally moved there from Japan.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:04.250
Fifty years ago, when my grandfather
was the first person to land on the moon,

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.790
he made first contact with aliens.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.500
What's the matter? Are you all right?

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.750
Chronic cramps...

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.080
When my grandfather helped that alien
who was suffering from cramps,

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.540
he signed over the alien moon base
on the other side of the moon to him.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:28.290
With that as a foundation, he made
a vast fortune trading with aliens

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:30.040
and founded a kingdom.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.000
Uh, there are so many things
I could say about that...

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:33.830
There are?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.750
Like, who was the alien he met on the moon?

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:38.660
And what's up with the chronic cramps?

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:41.330
I only ever heard that
they were chronic cramps.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.290
Hey, Robby, get a clue.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.200
In period dramas, you often see a girl
from town, dressed in a kimono,

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.160
slumped over by the side of the road.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.870
Then a passing samurai asks her,

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:54.040
"What's the matter?" and the
girl from town usually says,

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:55.750
"I have chronic cramping."

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:57.620
Sure, that's a staple of period dramas.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:01.540
According to my analysis, 90% of the time
when that happens, it's diarrhea.

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:02.830
That makes sense. I mean,

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.500
the girl from town isn't about to say
"I'm suffering from a case of loose stools"

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.290
to a samurai that she's just meeting
for the first time, right?

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.580
Though, for my part, whether the
lady has the trots or is puking,

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.580
I'd be like "Everybody's okay!"

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:16.580
Lowlife scum.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:18.620
I...

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.450
I had my future decided for me
from the time I was born--

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:25.330
that I would be king someday.
That was my reason for living.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.040
But I ran away from home
because it was so stifling.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.200
That's when I met you, Robby.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.410
If you don't get off the
beaten path and run into stuff,

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:35.540
nothing unpredictable will ever happen.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:40.700
It came as a shock. I wanted to go see
a world I'd never imagined before.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.790
And so, back then...

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.540
Prince Hatchi!

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.370
Unks! What are you doing here?

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.370
I've been keeping an eye
on you this whole time!

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:56.200
This running-away-from-home
stunt is over now!

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.910
This whole time? "Stunt"?

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.290
Come on, back to the moon!

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:05.000
No! I'm... I'm going to bend some rails!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.700
Prince!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.790
I'd come that far because it's what I wanted.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:18.250
I didn't want it to end like that.
I wanted to feel my heart pounding.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.040
Hatchi...

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:23.370
Traveling with you has made
it pound. It's been thrilling.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:27.500
And I was ashamed of myself for all
the things I only knew through books.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:32.040
Until I saw things and experienced them
for myself, I wouldn't know the truth.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:37.330
Thank you, Robby, for bringing me
on this journey with you.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:38.790
I'm sorry!

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.080
You've come all this way
feeling the way you do,

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.450
but now they know where
you are because of me!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.370
Not to mention making you
pay all of that money...

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.410
But I promise, I'll pay it back!

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:51.200
I can't do anything about it now,
but I promise I'll pay you back!

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:54.700
I'm down on my knees!
I'm really, really, sorry!

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:55.950
Robby...

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.370
Wh-What was that?!

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:01.660
Crap! We're caught in a tractor beam!

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:06.250
Ha, I've caught you for good this time, Robby.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.790
Damn it, Yang doesn't know when to quit!

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:12.200
But your debt has been paid;
why is he still after you?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.330
Huh?

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.700
Ass-butt!

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:18.330
Heh-heh, why, indeed?

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:23.500
Robby, you belong to me now!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.870
What is their problem?! Stop interfering!

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:37.290
Ikku, now's our chance!

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.290
Got it!

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:39.830
What's that over there?

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:46.540
A hyperroad!

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:48.580
What's it doing here?

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:53.580
"Dontsu Inc."

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:55.250
It's a Dontsu ship?

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.950
So that's it! They have a secret route!

00:11:57.950 --> 00:11:59.830
Ikku, latch onto that ship!

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.040
Roger!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:06.830
Do you think this will work?

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:11.950
Hey, we finished our pilgrimage
to Isekandar. Providence is on our side.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.580
Let's bring a proper end to this journey.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:15.790
Yeah.

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:28.830
Hmph! If you come between me and love,

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:31.750
you can be bitten to death by my <i>shachihoko</i>!

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.410
Hey, where is Robby?!

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.370
--Actually...
--We lost sight of him.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.410
Damn it! Find him, now!

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.540
Who even knew there was
this hyperroad here?

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:47.080
We're out-of-this-world lucky, aren't we?

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.080
Fortune may be turning our way.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.200
Listen... Huh? What the hell?

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.370
This hyperroad is ridiculously fast!

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:59.120
We're flying right by the stage
station planets we visited.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:00.290
We're what?

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:01.750
Hey, what's that?

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:03.620
"Dontsu Private Hyperroad"

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:06.500
Hey, did you see that just now?

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:08.540
This is a Dontsu-exclusive...

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:12.290
...hyperroad between Earth and Isekandar!

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:16.500
Mr. Yang, there's some kind of hole ahead.

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:17.330
Hole?

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:20.660
Not so much a hole as an
entrance to a hyperroad.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.750
Robby no doubt entered that hole!

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.620
We're going to thrust ourselves
into that hole, as well!

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.370
--Yes, Mr. Yang!
--Yes, Mr. Yang!

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.080
Oh! In no time at all,
we're already at Haccone!

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.040
Damn it, what is Dontsu doing,

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:42.040
making us regular people take the
long way and spend so much money?!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:47.500
While they get to use this hyperroad
to come and go in a much shorter time.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.580
Then again, that's about what I figured.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:54.790
Still, if we keep going like this,
it will be a shortcut back to Earth, right?

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.080
Just this once, we have Dontsu to thank.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.790
I guess that's true.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.870
What kind of road could this be, Mr. Yang?

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:08.160
We're traveling at incredible speed, Mr. Yang.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:13.700
None of that matters! Robby is definitely
up ahead. Give us more speed!

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.620
--Yes, Mr. Yang!
--Yes, Mr. Yang!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.790
This is amazing! We're already
to the solar system!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:22.250
We'll reach Earth in one more minute!

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.160
That happened so fast,
I don't feel anything at all.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:28.080
Yeah, it doesn't feel a bit like
we've traveled anywhere.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:32.450
Surprisingly enough, Dontsu may
have a point in what they're doing.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:34.000
Heh-heh, yeah, maybe.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.950
Hey! Something's coming up from behind!

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:38.660
I found you, Robby!

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.160
Wah! Yang is coming after us!

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.660
Run!

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.040
Hey, out of my way!

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.660
Yikes! He's catching up!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.830
Almost there!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.580
We're almost to Earth!
I'm slamming all our energy into this!

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.830
What are you doing?! Increase our speed!

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:14.330
But if we go any faster...

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.200
...our engines...!

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:16.540
I don't want excuses!

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.290
--Yes, Mr. Yang!
--Yes, Mr. Yang!

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:23.200
It's no use! He's overtaking us!

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:25.330
Robby!

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:31.620
Robby!

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.040
Prince Hatchi!

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.790
Huh?! I've been rammed from behind!

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.040
Oh, no! We're getting
knocked off the hyperroad!

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:47.330
So what will happen?

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:49.750
There's no telling where
we're going to warp out!

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:53.540
What do you mean, there's no telling?
Me and Hatchi are going to Earth!

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:56.540
Because until we do, our journey isn't over!

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:57.910
Robby...

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:20.580
The giant spaceship that suddenly
appeared in the skies over Neo Tokyo

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:25.750
has sent a message over a space comm
signal stating they are about to attack.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.910
--We're so screwed!
--They are mysterious creatures
from outer space,

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:29.700
--Oh my god!
--not affiliated with the Galactic Union,

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:30.540
--Aiya!
--not affiliated with the Galactic Union,

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:31.750
--Aiya!
--and say that their purpose
is to "assimilate" the Earth.

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.660
--Oh la la!
--and say that their purpose
is to "assimilate" the Earth.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:38.910
Are those of us on Earth
now doomed to perish?

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:44.370
The blast port is opening. We are now
facing Earth's last moments.

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:59.750
--Wah! Up ahead! We're falling!
--We're out!

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:00.580
Pull up, Ikku!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.830
I am!

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:04.870
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.120
Are we stuck in something?

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.580
Ikku, what happened?

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:11.450
It looks like we're inside
the tip of a huge structure.

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:13.290
There's an intense heat source dead ahead?!

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:14.950
Wait, could this be...?

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:16.620
We're in a whole world of trouble!

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:18.410
Run!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:39.250
Wh-What just happened? The giant
spaceship just blew itself up!

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:40.910
Wh-What is that?!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:47.950
What exactly could that be?! It's almost
like it's bathed in a golden aura...

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.790
Oh, that's...!

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:57.790
"He, clothed in golden robes,
shall descend from out of the flames."

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:03.000
This truly... This truly is the savior of Earth!

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.000
Whew, we somehow managed to escape.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:11.290
But what's up with all
this light? It's crazy bright.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:15.290
Ah, some new function was installed
when we were on Yokkamarché.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:18.040
It looks like whatever
it was acted as a barrier.

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.410
Oh...

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.250
That... is Hizakuriger.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:25.950
Hizakuriger?

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:30.830
Yeah. I saw him on TV when
I was a child. It's Hizakuriger!

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:35.330
Hey, there's something strange
going on down there.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:36.450
What?

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:48.250
Hizakuriger! Hizakuriger! Hizakuriger!

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:49.500
What is this?

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.120
Search me.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:54.370
Ah! The pilots of Hizakuriger have emerged!

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:57.370
They are indeed the great heroes
who have saved the Earth!

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.290
The saviors of mankind!

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:01.450
Huh? Wait, did we...

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.540
...just save...

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:04.580
--...the Earth?!
--...the Earth?!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.950
Seriously?

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:14.620
"Dontsu Inc."

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:17.120
What the hell just happened?!

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.450
It looks like we got wedged
into some building.

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:22.000
We've become some building's <i>shachihoko</i>.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:26.290
Just hurry up and get us out of here! Robby!

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.870
Excuse me! Over here, please!

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:36.160
--Okay.
--Over here, please!

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:38.830
I can really rock a back shot.

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:41.540
We are full-on Earth's heroes, huh?

00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:42.410
Yeah.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:47.330
I've had a ton of Grandpa's <i>Hizakuriger</i>
licensing agreements come to me.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.290
I can't take all of this!

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:54.450
I'll be able to pay what I owe you
in no time. In one lump sum!

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:56.500
I hope you're right.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:04.950
--Thank you very much!
--What is it?

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:09.790
Nothing. Good on us, right?
And all because we went to Isekandar.

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:11.080
You bet.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:17.120
It's the stone I picked up on Isekandar...

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:21.500
Ah! An Akafucrystal in the rough!

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:22.450
A real one?

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:26.950
Oh, so <i>that's </i>what happened!
It might all be thanks to this thing.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.870
Mm-hmm! It was worth going
to Isekandar for, huh?

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:32.370
Yeah. Here, take it.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:33.540
Huh?

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:39.250
Come on. Call it, you know,
a token of our trip together.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:45.500
Jeez! I said I'm giving it to you,
so hurry up and take it! Here!

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:46.950
A token, huh?

00:20:55.540 --> 00:21:00.290
Space--the final tourist spot.

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:04.000
There, we'll no doubt find epicurean
feats to stagger the imagination

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:08.870
and entirely new activities waiting for us!

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:50.250
"Hizakuriger Returns"

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:59.580
"Hizakuriger Robo sold out"
"One Ikku per customer"

00:22:54.160 --> 00:23:00.450
"RobiHachi: The Men Who Saved Earth"

00:23:18.160 --> 00:23:23.580
I never expected the Hizakuriger
bubble to burst so quickly.

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:26.660
I'm back to being penniless again.

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:33.120
What's wrong, Robby? You really are
hopeless without me along, aren't you?

00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:35.250
Hatchi, Ikku...

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:42.040
How about we go off once again
to find some happiness?

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:44.120
On a new journey!

00:23:45.120 --> 00:23:46.750
Yeah!

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:52.580
"The episode of RobiHachi you just enjoyed
is the last one. Thanks for watching."

00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:57.200
"The episode of RobiHachi you just enjoyed
is the last one. Thanks for watching."
♪ Let's go to Izumondar!
Let's go to Izumondar! ♪

00:23:57.200 --> 00:23:58.830
"So, where should they go
on their next journey?"
♪ Let's go to Izumondar!
Let's go to Izumondar! ♪

00:23:58.830 --> 00:23:59.200
"So, where should they go
on their next journey?"
♪ Izumon is a great place! ♪

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:02.040
"To the matchmaking planet of Izumondar?"
♪ Izumon is a great place! ♪

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:05.200
"Won't you take your own journey
beyond expectations?"
"See you somewhere out in the universe!"
♪ Let's go to Izumondar! ♪

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:06.950
"Won't you take your own journey
beyond expectations?"
"See you somewhere out in the universe!"
♪ Come on, let's go! ♪
